[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
No outage is present on Location C (192.168.200.0/24). Layer-2 and gateway reachability are healthy, and inter-site routing is working. From each affected host we verified:
- Local gateway: pc11→192.168.200.1 (router4) 3/3 replies, ~0.70 ms; pc12/pc13/pc14 show identical success (0% loss).
- Same-subnet: pc11→pc12 3/3 replies (0% loss), confirming Location C switching works.
- Other sites: pc11→pc5 (172.16.10.5) succeeds (0% loss), as do pc12–pc14 to the same remote host in the automated matrix.

On the gateway, router4’s interface toward Location C is correctly configured and up:
- router4 eth0 = 192.168.200.1/24 (state UP/LOWER_UP), responding to ICMP.
- Routing on router4 is present (default via 172.25.1.2, and multiple remote prefixes learned via RIP), and Location C’s connected route 192.168.200.0/24 is active on eth0.

Mechanism: If Location C were isolated, pings to the local gateway would fail and inter-site probes would drop; instead, we observe 0% loss locally and across sites. This localizes healthy operation to switch5/switch6 and router4 eth0, with working upstream paths.

Root cause: No network fault observed; the reported isolation condition is not occurring at this time.

Corrective fix: None required. If users still see issues, investigate host-specific problems (firewall, app/DNS) or capture failing endpoints/timestamps to correlate, but the network segment and gateway are operating normally. 
